  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "InternReadFile",
    "file": "assimp/code/AssetLib/OFF/OFFLoader.cpp",
    "description": "The OFF loader trusts the declared face count when allocating and assigning mesh->mNumFaces. If GetNextLine() reaches an embedded NUL/end-of-input before all declared faces are parsed, the face loop only logs and breaks (lines 277-280) without rejecting the file or reducing mNumFaces to the number actually initialized. This propagates default aiFace entries with mNumIndices == 0. With this PoV, later triangulation/primitive preprocessing leaves a mixed-type mesh, and SortByPTypeProcess::Execute classifies every face using aiNumPerPType[pFirstFace->mNumIndices - 1]; a zero-index trailing face unsigned-underflows the array index and causes the wild write at SortByPTypeProcess.cpp:189.",
    "conditions": "A memory-loaded OFF file must declare a positive face count larger than the number of face lines actually available; an embedded NUL or premature EOF makes GetNextLine() fail during the face loop. At least one parsed nonempty polygon plus the uninitialized trailing zero-index faces must survive through the TargetRealtime_Quality post-processing pipeline so the mesh requires primitive-type splitting. The supplied input declares 1 vertex and 7 faces but terminates face data early, leaving zero-count aiFace objects that reach SortByPTypeProcess."
  },
